TI  - Tree of Attacks: Jailbreaking Black-Box LLMs Automatically
AU  - Anay Mehrotra
AU  - Manolis Zampetakis
AU  - Paul Kassianik
AU  - Blaine Nelson
AU  - Hyrum Anderson
AU  - Yaron Singer
AU  - Amin Karbasi
PY  - 2024
AB  - While Large Language Models (LLMs) display versatile functionality, they continue to generate harmful, biased, and toxic content, as demonstrated by the prevalence of human-designedjailbreaks. In this work, we presentTree of Attacks with Pruning(TAP), an automated method for generating jailbreaks that only requires black-box access to the target LLM. TAP utilizes an attacker LLM to iteratively refine candidate (attack) prompts until one of the refined prompts jailbreaks the target. In addition, before sending prompts to the target, TAP assesses them and prunes the ones unlikely to result in jailbreaks, reducing the number of queries sent to the target LLM. In empirical evaluations, we observe that TAP generates prompts that jailbreak state-of-the-art LLMs (including GPT4-Turbo and GPT4o) for more than 80% of the prompts. This significantly improves upon the previous state-of-the-art black-box methods for generating jailbreaks while using a smaller number of queries than them. Furthermore, TAP is also capable of jailbreaking LLMs protected by state-of-the-artguardrails, e.g., LlamaGuard.
