TI  - CogVLM: Visual Expert for Pretrained Language Models
AU  - Weihan Wang
AU  - Qingsong Lv
AU  - Wenmeng Yu
AU  - Wenyi Hong
AU  - Ji Qi
AU  - Yan Wang
AU  - Junhui Ji
AU  - Zhuoyi Yang
AU  - Lei Zhao
AU  - Xixuan Song
AU  - Jiazheng Xu
AU  - Keqin Chen
AU  - Bin Xu
AU  - Juanzi Li
AU  - Yuxiao Dong
AU  - Ming Ding
AU  - Jie Tang
PY  - 2024
AB  - We introduce CogVLM, a powerful open-source visual language foundation model. Different from the popular \emph{shallow alignment} method which maps image features into the input space of language model, CogVLM bridges the gap between the frozen pretrained language model and image encoder by a trainable visual expert module in the attention and FFN layers. As a result, CogVLM enables a deep fusion of vision language features without sacrificing any performance on NLP tasks. CogVLM-17B achieves state-of-the-art performance on 17 classic cross-modal benchmarks, including 1) image captioning datasets: NoCaps, Flicker30k, 2) VQA datasets: OKVQA, TextVQA, OCRVQA, ScienceQA, 3) LVLM benchmarks: MM-Vet, MMBench, SEED-Bench, LLaVABench, POPE, MMMU, MathVista, 4) visual grounding datasets: RefCOCO, RefCOCO+, RefCOCOg, Visual7W. Codes and checkpoints are available at Github.
